2025-12-03 15:27:20,345 - [Quantum_e2e_20251202_nova_z_R18all_2.py:316] - [get_register_document] - INFO - 获取到的result_text: {"jobId":65,"status":"complete","data":{"text":"[{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:15:38.828\",\"description\":\"This paper explores factorial properties of subrings within commutative rings, focusing on irreducible and square-free elements and their connection to Jacobian conditions. It studies subrings R of polynomial rings A=k[x1,...,xn], generated by algebraically independent polynomials, and examines a generalized Jacobian Conjecture: if the greatest common divisor (gcd) of certain Jacobian determinants is a nonzero constant from k, then R is algebraically closed in A. Key results relate gcd conditions to inclusion relations between irreducible and square-free elements (IrrR ⊆ SqfA, SqfR ⊆ SqfA). The concept of square-factorially closed subrings is introduced, equating certain inclusions to root closedness. The paper establishes conditions under which divisibility, associativity, and relative primeness in subrings correspond to those in their ambient rings, with explicit equivalences and counterexamples demonstrating limits of these relationships. Several factorial closure properties are presented, including B-factorial and self-factorial closure, and their implications for algebraic closedness and separability in positive characteristic. The authors develop a diagram outlining the relations among prime, irreducible, square-free, radical, and generator elements between subrings and ambient rings. Multiple propositions establish equivalences between various factorial forms and their consequences, highlighting that such closure properties do not necessarily imply unique factorization. The results have relevance for polynomial rings, locally nilpotent derivations, and rings of constants. References provide further foundational work on root closure, Keller maps, polynomial derivations, and Jacobian conditions.\",\"docName\":\"1606.06592\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:16:09.255\",\"fileName\":\"1606.06592.docx\",\"fileType\":\"docx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116099527217152\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Data Analysis\",\"Research Paper\",\"Science\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"ef2ddfdd9388f3ce77214c0c197dba17\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\1606.06592.docx\",\"priority\":\"1\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"9b75c861-dd6b-449b-85c7-a48faa422108\",\"tokenNum\":\"7840\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:16:07.687\",\"description\":\"The Mortgage Lenders and Administrators Statistics for Q1 2014, compiled by the Bank of England and FCA, report residential loan amounts outstanding at £1,243 billion, up 0.4% from Q4 2013. Regulated loans comprised 79% (£978.5 billion); non-regulated loans rose to £264.4 billion. Securitised loan balances declined to £101.3 billion, marking the lowest proportion (8.1%) since 2007. New business saw gross advances of £47.1 billion, up 38.5% year-on-year but down 8.5% from the previous quarter. Net advances dropped to £7.0 billion, while new commitments were £48.8 billion, a 37.5% annual rise. Fixed-rate loans reached a record 81.0% of gross advances; average interest rates fell to all-time lows (gross advances: 3.24%, balances: 3.34%). Lending for house purchases was 66.4%; first-time buyers accounted for 20.1%, remortgages for 27.4%, and buy-to-let lending grew to 14.4%. High LTV (>90%) lending rose to 3.6%. Arrears and possessions improved: new arrears cases fell 5%, and possession cases dropped 17.4% year-on-year, both reaching the lowest levels since 2007. Performance of loans in arrears increased for the seventh consecutive quarter. The data reflect the joint regulatory environment post-PRA/FCA creation and offer details on lending criteria, securitisation, interest rates, and arrears definitions. Technical notes clarify reporting standards and data interpretation for further analysis.\",\"docName\":\"2016 -FCA UK Financial Conduct Authority_mlar_statistics_june_2014_commentary_10页_384kb(1)\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:16:15.307\",\"fileName\":\"2016 -FCA UK Financial Conduct Authority_mlar_statistics_june_2014_commentary_10页_384kb(1).pptx\",\"fileType\":\"pptx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116220570636288\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Finance\",\"Data Analysis\",\"Report\",\"Finance\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"b0d49940e25353f97dae255fe9f5146d\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\2016 -FCA UK Financial Conduct Authority_mlar_statistics_june_2014_commentary_10页_384kb(1).pptx\",\"priority\":\"2\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"fcea78dd-d710-4f04-abe7-9d9758ec64f1\",\"tokenNum\":\"8466\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:16:14.022\",\"description\":\"The document lists societies prosecuted under the Co-operative and Community Benefit Societies Act 2014 for failing to submit required annual returns. It provides society registration numbers, names, hearing dates, and the outcome of proceedings, including fines and conditional discharges. Notable societies mentioned include Newtown National Club Limited, Pantyffynnon Social Club and Insurance Limited, and Bromley United Services Club Limited. The main penalties imposed were monetary fines ranging from £200 to £1,500, primarily for non-submission of annual returns for financial years 2012 to 2014. Some societies received conditional discharges instead of fines. Each case's specific details, such as the relevant years of omitted returns and corresponding financial penalties, are noted. The summary underscores the enforcement actions taken to ensure compliance with statutory financial reporting requirements under the 2014 Act.\",\"docName\":\"2016 -FCA UK Financial Conduct Authority_societies_prosecuted_2015_1页_71kb\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:16:18.785\",\"fileName\":\"2016 -FCA UK Financial Conduct Authority_societies_prosecuted_2015_1页_71kb.pptx\",\"fileType\":\"pptx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116247141552128\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Report\",\"Legal\",\"Compliance\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"86f78a8c6314435414f5c27f87e78e23\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\2016 -FCA UK Financial Conduct Authority_societies_prosecuted_2015_1页_71kb.pptx\",\"priority\":\"3\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"78b6cd1e-a5b2-4e6e-9c84-c68527af8eeb\",\"tokenNum\":\"271\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:16:18.128\",\"description\":\"This article analyzes female participation and performance in computer science (CS) in England, particularly after the 2014 curriculum reform that replaced Information and Communication Technology (ICT) with a more programming-focused CS subject. Using the 2016 national pupil database (over 5 million students, ~60,000 in CS), it finds a decline in female representation in CS (20% at GCSE, 10% at A-level) compared to ICT and highlights a relative underrepresentation of both girls and working-class students. Notably, females from poorer areas were more likely to take CS than those from wealthier areas, a trend not seen among boys. Ethnic minority females were better represented in CS than white females, though overall participation and attainment were higher in ICT. Girls typically received higher raw grades in CS than boys; however, after controlling for general academic ability, boys outperformed girls in CS by 0.31 of a grade. Female underperformance was strongest in schools with larger female CS cohorts, especially in mixed-gender schools. All-girls schools saw better female outcomes, but offered CS less frequently. The shift from ICT to CS may negatively impact female self-efficacy and future choices in computing due to perceived difficulty and existing sociocultural stereotypes. The article advocates that curriculum designers and teachers prioritize inclusivity and consider diverse qualifications to counteract declining female participation and relative underperformance in computing.\",\"docName\":\"2016_GCSE_Gender-FINAL-author (1)\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:16:58.161\",\"fileName\":\"2016_GCSE_Gender-FINAL-author (1).docx\",\"fileType\":\"docx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116264363364352\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Data Analysis\",\"Research Paper\",\"Education\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"e4ab13cf85164f1df78f49137304feea\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\2016_GCSE_Gender-FINAL-author (1).docx\",\"priority\":\"4\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"cfe74278-f414-4710-802b-5d18fec7548b\",\"tokenNum\":\"30593\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:16:54.884\",\"description\":\"This research investigates how the presence or absence of prompts affects the accuracy of zero-shot detectors for identifying AI-generated text. Zero-shot detectors, which typically work without additional training data and are often based on likelihood scores, have become popular tools for distinguishing human-written from AI-generated content. However, these detectors usually analyze texts in isolation, neglecting the prompt context used during generation, which can impact detection reliability. The paper empirically compares 'white-box' detection (detectors have access to the original prompts) against 'black-box' detection (detectors do not use prompts), using multiple likelihood-based methods including DetectGPT, FastDetectGPT, LRR, NPR, and Binoculars. Experimental results demonstrate a significant decline in detection accuracy for all methods in black-box settings, with AUC scores dropping by at least 0.1. Fast series detectors and Binoculars show greater robustness. The study also finds that increasing token replacement ratios and sample sizes can partially mitigate accuracy loss but not entirely eliminate it. The findings are relevant to both malicious and benign prompt scenarios and have implications for related tasks like paraphrase generation, supervised detection, and watermarking. The paper suggests that combining autoregressive with masked language model representations or other features could yield more robust detectors. Practical recommendations include considering prompt information for improved AI text detection and further research into longer texts, varied tasks, and the resilience of different model sizes.\",\"docName\":\"2403.20127\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:07.879\",\"fileName\":\"2403.20127.pdf\",\"fileType\":\"pdf\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116418529202176\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Data Analysis\",\"Research Paper\",\"Technology\",\"Technology\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"90fea7f382da6ed4acd99903f65d38ee\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\2403.20127.pdf\",\"priority\":\"5\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"c2e24149-4057-49d5-a557-c78b01f8cc76\",\"tokenNum\":\"8241\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:06.312\",\"description\":\"Tuscany is a central Italian region with a population of about 3.8 million (2013), and its capital is Florence. Renowned for its landscapes, traditions, historical significance, and cultural influence, Tuscany is considered the birthplace of the Italian Renaissance and has notable artistic and scientific heritage. Major museums include the Uffizi and Pitti Palace. Tuscany is famous for its wines such as Chianti and Brunello di Montalcino and is recognized for a strong regional identity. It is a top tourist destination, with Florence, Pisa, Montecatini Terme, Castiglione della Pescaia, and Grosseto being the most popular in 2014. Seaside tourism, particularly in Castiglione della Pescaia, constitutes 40% of tourist arrivals. Other prominent areas include Siena, Lucca, Chianti, Versilia, and Val d'Orcia. Tuscany hosts seven UNESCO World Heritage Sites, including the historic centers of Florence, San Gimignano, Siena, Pienza, Val d'Orcia, and more. The region also features over 120 protected nature reserves, which, along with its cultural assets, draw millions of tourists annually; Florence alone welcomed over 1.8 million visitors in 2012, ranking as the 89th most visited city globally.\",\"docName\":\"31uv0mxwnqc77o5jzgp1cp15oz95ic\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:13.493\",\"fileName\":\"31uv0mxwnqc77o5jzgp1cp15oz95ic.txt\",\"fileType\":\"txt\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116466461708288\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Informational\",\"History\",\"Report\",\"Informational\",\"History\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"6d2ca0adfa2c5021d9c38b226ca4badc\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\31uv0mxwnqc77o5jzgp1cp15oz95ic.txt\",\"priority\":\"6\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"0eb32b68-1ddd-496d-8258-068b25368d15\",\"tokenNum\":\"436\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:12.262\",\"description\":\"In this scene set at Hellingsley, Lady Wallinger and her niece, Edith, are spending a peaceful morning together; Edith arranges flowers while Lady Wallinger embroiders. Conversation centers around Mr. Coningsby, expressing deep admiration for his character and recalling fond memories of meeting him in Paris and Cambridge. Lady Wallinger emphasizes her high regard for Coningsby, considering him superior to other young men and Edith's best admirer. Edith shares her enjoyment in arranging roses, referencing Mr. Coningsby's thoughtful bouquets. Meanwhile, Oswald (Edith’s brother) and Sir Joseph are busy at the stables, and Mr. Millbank has not yet arrived from the factories. The tone is one of reflection and appreciation for Coningsby's qualities and the happiness his companionship brings, particularly to Oswald. The passage highlights familial bonds, aesthetic pleasure, and the esteem held for a central character.\",\"docName\":\"32riadziss4e5j4fqn05bz1ex1p4s7\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:18.349\",\"fileName\":\"32riadziss4e5j4fqn05bz1ex1p4s7.txt\",\"fileType\":\"txt\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116491417817088\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Informational\",\"History\",\"Text Document\",\"Informational\",\"History\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"407011444160e5c581548a18b3e52c54\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\32riadziss4e5j4fqn05bz1ex1p4s7.txt\",\"priority\":\"7\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"c04293df-6d13-415e-9569-4a9df8b489c9\",\"tokenNum\":\"410\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:17.534\",\"description\":\"Climate refers to the long-term statistics of weather in a region, determined by patterns in variables such as temperature, humidity, atmospheric pressure, wind, precipitation, and particle count. Unlike weather, which is short-term, climate examines these factors over extended periods. The climate system consists of five major components: atmosphere, hydrosphere, cryosphere, lithosphere, and biosphere. Factors influencing a region’s climate include latitude, terrain, altitude, and proximity to water bodies and currents. Climate classifications, such as the Köppen and Thornthwaite systems, utilize variables like temperature, precipitation, and evapotranspiration, aiding in the study of biodiversity and the impact of climate change. Other classification methods, like Bergeron and Spatial Synoptic systems, consider the origin of air masses. Paleoclimatology investigates ancient climates using proxy data from sources such as sediments, ice cores, tree rings, and corals, as direct measurements are only available since the 19th century. Climate models use mathematical simulations to study past, present, and future climates. Climate change operates on varying timescales, with recent trends including global warming, which shifts climate zones. For instance, a 3°C increase in mean annual temperature can move isotherms 300–400 km in latitude or 500 m in elevation, leading to species migration towards higher latitudes or elevations.\",\"docName\":\"336yqze83vet37vakvnt4i8m5645mz\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:25.056\",\"fileName\":\"336yqze83vet37vakvnt4i8m5645mz.txt\",\"fileType\":\"txt\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116513530187776\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Informational\",\"Research Paper\",\"Informational\",\"Science\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"13ddbd7a7dcfa75d8e7662e9eebffc47\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\336yqze83vet37vakvnt4i8m5645mz.txt\",\"priority\":\"8\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"eb3e822a-1d09-4a27-a8d0-0c625dd0149a\",\"tokenNum\":\"415\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:24.093\",\"description\":\"Spike Lee's 1989 film 'Do the Right Thing' was initially met with fears from critics and commentators that it would incite violence and negatively impact race relations, with some speculating it could affect David Dinkins's mayoral campaign and cause riots. Contrary to these predictions, the film generated significant public discussion but no violence, and Dinkins was elected mayor. The movie had considerable box office success and received two Academy Award nominations. Over time, 'Do the Right Thing' has been recognized as a seminal work, earning a spot on the American Film Institute's list of the 100 best American films in 2007. Renowned critic Roger Ebert praised the film for its empathetic portrayal of racial issues and lauded Lee's directorial achievement. The film's lasting impact is attributed to its visual boldness, confident direction, and its powerful, realistic depiction of social tensions. Lee's previous films had already established him as a notable filmmaker, but 'Do the Right Thing,' made when he was 32, solidified his reputation through its stylistic choices and commentary on American race relations.\",\"docName\":\"35gcefq6i5oqoz7pl1puxn6b53o3zu\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:31.007\",\"fileName\":\"35gcefq6i5oqoz7pl1puxn6b53o3zu.txt\",\"fileType\":\"txt\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116541040627712\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"History\",\"Report\",\"History\",\"Art & Design\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"875798ebdbaf9e76099f7b98829887c8\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\35gcefq6i5oqoz7pl1puxn6b53o3zu.txt\",\"priority\":\"9\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"900bf6fb-2c1b-4351-a939-75e1c451ddaf\",\"tokenNum\":\"419\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:30.198\",\"description\":\"Dennis Farina, a former Chicago police officer turned actor, passed away at age 69. Renowned for his tough, charismatic screen presence, Farina was best known for roles in TV series such as 'Law & Order,' 'Crime Story,' and 'Miami Vice.' He often portrayed law enforcement or gangster figures, informed by his real-life policing background. Farina began acting after director Michael Mann cast him in 'Thief' (1981) and continued as a regular in Mann’s productions, notably starring as Lt. Mike Torello in 'Crime Story.' His film career included notable performances in 'Midnight Run' (1988), 'Get Shorty' (1995), 'The Mod Squad' (1999), and 'Snatch' (2000). In 2004, Farina joined 'Law & Order,' playing Detective Joe Fontana, a character celebrated for his stylish appearance, contrasting with previous detectives on the show. He worked alongside Jesse L. Martin until leaving after two years. Farina was remembered as professional, humorous, and passionate by colleagues and his publicist, Lori De Waal. He will be missed by family, friends, and the entertainment community.\",\"docName\":\"36v4q8r5zk0iwte84nbw2t3d0qzqmg\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:37.744\",\"fileName\":\"36v4q8r5zk0iwte84nbw2t3d0qzqmg.txt\",\"fileType\":\"txt\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116566646853632\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"History\",\"Report\",\"History\",\"Art & Design\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"a66d0da90f5c9480465e3a1565a8a4d5\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\36v4q8r5zk0iwte84nbw2t3d0qzqmg.txt\",\"priority\":\"10\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"a28408bb-8228-40e1-b42a-744ce98730b8\",\"tokenNum\":\"386\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:36.713\",\"description\":\"The Chicago Tribune, established in 1847 by James Kelly, John E. Wheeler, and Joseph K. C. Forrest, is a prominent daily newspaper based in Chicago, Illinois, currently owned by Tronc, Inc. It is the most widely read newspaper in the Chicago metropolitan area and Great Lakes region and ranks as the eighth-largest U.S. newspaper by circulation. The Tribune once branded itself as the 'World’s Greatest Newspaper,' influencing the names of WGN radio and television. Traditionally a broadsheet, the paper experimented with a tabloid format for certain sales channels between 2009 and 2011, but reverted to broadsheet due to reader feedback. Its masthead features the American flag as a nod to its past motto, 'An American Paper for Americans,' though the motto has since been removed. Politically, the Tribune began as unaffiliated but leaned toward anti-Democratic stances, supporting Whig and Free Soil parties, and by the 1850s, published nativist and temperance editorials. In 1855, it formally aligned with the nativist American (Know Nothing) party, aiding in the election of Levi Boone as Chicago mayor. The paper underwent several changes in ownership and editorship during its early years.\",\"docName\":\"3atpcq38j8aq3uw5yu2l6obf6w8yah\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:44.133\",\"fileName\":\"3atpcq38j8aq3uw5yu2l6obf6w8yah.txt\",\"fileType\":\"txt\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116593972744192\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Informational\",\"History\",\"Report\",\"Informational\",\"History\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"e135fab2784631c3dc428ca3ada56095\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\3atpcq38j8aq3uw5yu2l6obf6w8yah.txt\",\"priority\":\"11\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"a32a115b-48ac-430a-a80e-1c7900d62fe0\",\"tokenNum\":\"441\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:43.110\",\"description\":\"Scientists have developed a technique using laser-induced breakdown spectroscopy to identify the geographic origin of precious gemstones such as diamonds, emeralds, and rubies. Spearheaded by Catherine McManus at Materialytics, the method analyzes light patterns produced when a powerful laser turns a tiny sample of gemstone into plasma, with each light pattern reflecting the stone's elemental signature. Comparing these patterns against a growing database allows matching an unknown gem to its source, potentially pinpointing not just the country but the exact mine of origin. The technique demonstrated high accuracy, correctly identifying 95% of diamonds and 98% of emeralds and rubies in tests. This advancement is crucial due to regulatory requirements following a 2010 U.S. law mandating verification of gemstone origins, aimed at reducing the trade in so-called 'blood minerals' from conflict zones. The tool could improve ethical sourcing by helping companies comply with these laws and mitigating the funding of civil wars linked to gemstone sales. Although promising, the method will require further data collection from diverse gem sources before broad commercial deployment. Experts in mineralogy, like Barbara Dutrow, recognize the potential of this technique as a significant advancement in gemstone identification and ethical sourcing.\",\"docName\":\"3bxqmrhwkzyaomlplwv1cu024ijumi\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:50.425\",\"fileName\":\"3bxqmrhwkzyaomlplwv1cu024ijumi.txt\",\"fileType\":\"txt\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116620803706880\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Research Paper\",\"Compliance\",\"Science\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"84d98a88990202d6460cfb1be589ff80\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\3bxqmrhwkzyaomlplwv1cu024ijumi.txt\",\"priority\":\"12\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"832a21e1-9fb5-40f6-b597-d73fcf149015\",\"tokenNum\":\"617\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:49.633\",\"description\":\"The Arena Football League (AFL), founded in 1987 by Jim Foster, is the premier professional indoor American football league in the United States and the third longest-running professional football league in North America. Games are played indoors on a smaller, 68-yard field, offering a faster-paced and higher-scoring experience compared to traditional football. Originally invented and patented by Foster in the early 1980s, the AFL consisted of 12 U.S.-based teams during its 2015 season. During the season, the league took control of two teams, but later ceased their operations immediately, resulting in the cancellation and tie declaration of a scheduled game between them. The Spokane Shock also left the AFL for the Indoor Football League (IFL) soon after. The AFL is organized into two conferences—American and National. By the start of the 2016 season, each conference was reduced to four teams, following the shutdown of the 2015 champion San Jose SaberCats for reasons unrelated to league operations.\",\"docName\":\"3fe7txl1linsppafu5scnkpfvoq2qg\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:55.715\",\"fileName\":\"3fe7txl1linsppafu5scnkpfvoq2qg.txt\",\"fileType\":\"txt\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116648163151872\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"History\",\"Report\",\"History\",\"Sports\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"c64bcb2b87bb69f322bfba1cb38d4003\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\3fe7txl1linsppafu5scnkpfvoq2qg.txt\",\"priority\":\"13\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"a64aea9d-ea79-4917-a9c2-28273b159f8b\",\"tokenNum\":\"277\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:17:54.749\",\"description\":\"Slovenia, officially the Republic of Slovenia, is a nation in southern Central Europe, at the intersection of key European cultural and trade routes. It borders Italy, Austria, Hungary, Croatia, and the Adriatic Sea, and has a population of 2.06 million. The country is primarily mountainous, with diverse climates ranging from continental to Alpine and sub-Mediterranean. Slovenia features significant biodiversity, abundant water resources, and over half of its land is forested. Human settlement is spread unevenly across the territory. Historically, Slovenia has been influenced by various European cultures and languages, though the majority population is Slovene and Slovene is the official language. While largely secular, Slovenian culture has deep Catholic and Lutheran influences. Politically, Slovenia is a parliamentary republic and a member of the United Nations, European Union, and NATO. Economically, Slovenia relies on an export-oriented, small, and open economy, with the services sector being the largest, followed by industry and construction. The Slovenian economy was notably impacted by the Eurozone crisis of the late 2000s.\",\"docName\":\"3gu1kf0o4i11dq9wdl6yo829k9tpbc\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:18:02.369\",\"fileName\":\"3gu1kf0o4i11dq9wdl6yo829k9tpbc.txt\",\"fileType\":\"txt\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116669621211136\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Informational\",\"History\",\"Report\",\"Informational\",\"History\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"fcee447757ecf34af39348fb43e3c75f\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\3gu1kf0o4i11dq9wdl6yo829k9tpbc.txt\",\"priority\":\"14\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"7f360644-45ee-4697-b5a1-8d06c2236827\",\"tokenNum\":\"405\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:18:01.199\",\"description\":\"A One Day International (ODI) is a limited overs cricket match played between two international teams, typically with each side facing 50 overs. The format, considered the highest standard for List A cricket, was first played on 5 January 1971 between Australia and England after a Test match was abandoned. Initially, ODIs featured white uniforms and a red ball, but significant changes occurred in the late 1970s during Kerry Packer's World Series Cricket. Innovations introduced included coloured uniforms, night matches under floodlights with a white ball, and enhanced television coverage using multiple cameras, pitch microphones, and on-screen graphics. The first match with coloured kits was played in 1979. These changes contributed to increased professionalism, as players began receiving salaries and focusing solely on cricket. The transition to coloured clothing and a white ball in ODIs became standard, and white flannels with a red ball were phased out by 2001. The Cricket World Cup uses this format, which remains a prominent aspect of international cricket.\",\"docName\":\"3nql1cs15r8aviz39pth2bpsr4zvy1\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:18:07.964\",\"fileName\":\"3nql1cs15r8aviz39pth2bpsr4zvy1.txt\",\"fileType\":\"txt\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116696674471936\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Informational\",\"History\",\"Informational\",\"History\",\"Sport\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"da0c0f7162b267cca0de596df4c40c56\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\3nql1cs15r8aviz39pth2bpsr4zvy1.txt\",\"priority\":\"15\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"35229ecd-3da0-46ee-bb96-3602fe668cb8\",\"tokenNum\":\"402\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:18:06.727\",\"description\":\"Staten Island, one of New York City’s five boroughs, is the southernmost part of both the city and the state of New York. Bordered by Arthur Kill, Kill Van Kull, and New York Bay, Staten Island is coextensive with Richmond County and was known as the Borough of Richmond until 1975. With a 2016 estimated population of 476,015, Staten Island is the least populated borough but the third largest in area. It is distinctive for its non-Hispanic White majority population. Often referred to as 'the forgotten borough' due to perceived neglect by city government, Staten Island features diverse regions: the urban North Shore with notable historic districts and Victorian architecture; the East Shore, home to the F.D.R. Boardwalk, the world’s fourth-longest boardwalk; the rapidly suburbanized South Shore, initially settled by Dutch and French Huguenots in the 17th century; and the West Shore, which is mostly industrial and sparsely populated. The borough’s flag and identity reflect its historic ties as Richmond County.\",\"docName\":\"3tayzsbpll8425psm9hhik4gdl02sc\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:18:13.323\",\"fileName\":\"3tayzsbpll8425psm9hhik4gdl02sc.txt\",\"fileType\":\"txt\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116719860584448\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Informational\",\"History\",\"Report\",\"Informational\",\"History\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"bbab72be59f8af894a739f11b9da46ff\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\3tayzsbpll8425psm9hhik4gdl02sc.txt\",\"priority\":\"16\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"fc0eb33b-1fe9-42d2-b335-b22c65bf87ef\",\"tokenNum\":\"344\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:18:11.808\",\"description\":\"Since its inception in 1956, the Eurovision Song Contest has seen participation from fifty-two countries, with twenty-seven securing victories. Organized annually by the European Broadcasting Union (EBU), the contest is open to active EBU broadcasters, irrespective of geographical boundaries within Europe or EU membership. Notably, several non-European countries have competed: Israel (since 1973), Cyprus (since 1981), Armenia (since 2006), Morocco (in 1980), and Australia (debut in 2015, with subsequent entries in 2016 and 2017). Transcontinental countries with partial European territory—Turkey, Russia, Georgia, and Azerbaijan—also participate. Past interest in joining the competition has come from Lebanon, Tunisia, and Qatar, though none have ultimately competed, with Qatar's interest in 2009 not resulting in an entry. The contest’s eligibility emphasizes membership in the EBU or the Council of Europe, allowing a diverse range of countries to participate beyond the European continent.\",\"docName\":\"3uouji6mtdeliyktz3xanbg0bugxuy\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:18:19.090\",\"fileName\":\"3uouji6mtdeliyktz3xanbg0bugxuy.txt\",\"fileType\":\"txt\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116741171843072\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Informational\",\"History\",\"Report\",\"Informational\",\"History\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"f51a9c4166febc0c1fda3580e29936a8\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\3uouji6mtdeliyktz3xanbg0bugxuy.txt\",\"priority\":\"17\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"1cb73712-01a3-4451-bd9c-149874fabe4c\",\"tokenNum\":\"408\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:18:18.037\",\"description\":\"Discogs is a crowdsourced online database and website dedicated to cataloging audio recordings, including commercial, promotional, and unofficial releases. Specializing in electronic music and vinyl records, Discogs comprises over 8 million releases from nearly 4.9 million artists, across 1 million labels, with constant data contributions from a community of about 346,000 users. Launched in November 2000 by Kevin Lewandowski, Discogs was initially focused on electronic music inspired by successful community-driven platforms. The site is operated by Zink Media, Inc. in Portland, Oregon. Initially exclusive to electronic music, the database expanded between 2004 and 2007 to include a wide range of genres such as hip hop, rock, jazz, funk/soul, Latin, reggae, blues, classical, non-music, and more, enabling comprehensive coverage of nearly every type of audio recording ever released.\",\"docName\":\"3z2r0dq0jhe3smkalexct301cwae2a\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:18:24.482\",\"fileName\":\"3z2r0dq0jhe3smkalexct301cwae2a.txt\",\"fileType\":\"txt\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116767298162688\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Informational\",\"Technology\",\"Technology\",\"Informational\",\"Database\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"7b1fc62222765d710e28c69beec63c3d\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\3z2r0dq0jhe3smkalexct301cwae2a.txt\",\"priority\":\"18\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"7dcfaccd-e285-4a59-a7a4-6a96fa2fe804\",\"tokenNum\":\"433\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:18:23.032\",\"description\":\"The EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) Compliance Policy of Georgia College outlines the lawful basis and procedures for collecting and processing personal and sensitive personal data in compliance with EU GDPR requirements. The policy applies to all Georgia College units handling such data and mandates a specific, documented lawful basis, including consent, contractual necessity, legal obligations, or legitimate interests. Sensitive personal data requires explicit, demonstrable consent, which can be withdrawn at any time with a straightforward process. The policy guarantees rights to data subjects such as transparency, access, rectification, erasure, objection to processing, and data portability. Georgia College must provide privacy notices specifying the categories of data collected, purposes, recipients, retention periods, and complaint procedures. All data handling and security measures must adhere to NIST SP 800-171 standards, and any suspected data breaches must be reported immediately to the Office of Legal Affairs. Responsible parties, including College Units, Legal Affairs, and Cyber Security, have defined roles in data governance, breach notification, and responding to inquiries. The policy aims to ensure consistent GDPR compliance, data security, and protection of individuals’ rights related to their personal information processed by the university. Effective from May 2018, the policy is subject to ongoing review and updates as needed.\",\"docName\":\"518_gulation Compliance Policy Statement\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:18:32.004\",\"fileName\":\"518_gulation Compliance Policy Statement.pdf\",\"fileType\":\"pdf\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116788248711168\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Legal\",\"Policy\",\"Compliance\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"ab418e6536b4d3edef622a23f2147d53\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\518_gulation Compliance Policy Statement.pdf\",\"priority\":\"19\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"7455e743-da0e-4224-9bf5-4027dd5b8377\",\"tokenNum\":\"2734\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:18:30.936\",\"description\":\"This paper analyzes leverage by distinguishing between financing leverage (arising from borrowing funds in capital markets) and operating liability leverage (arising from transactions with suppliers, customers, or employees). It develops explicit equations showing how each leverage type affects shareholder profitability (return on common equity, ROCE), operating profitability (RNOA), and ultimately price-to-book (P/B) ratios. Financing leverage impacts ROCE via the spread between operating returns and borrowing costs, while operating liability leverage enhances RNOA and, through both real and accounting effects, influences both present and future profitability as well as P/B ratios. Empirical analysis of over 63,000 U.S. firm-year observations (1963–2001) confirms that the market prices operating and financing liabilities differently. Operating liabilities—especially distinctions between contractual (e.g., accounts payable) and estimated accrual-based liabilities (e.g., deferred revenues, pension obligations)—are strong predictors of both current and future profitability, as well as valuation multiples. Conservative accrual estimates can depress current profits but raise future returns and affect equity pricing. These findings have implications for financial statement analysis, investment valuation, and earnings forecasting, arguing for a nuanced approach to liability classification. The study recommends further research on line-item details and industry circumstances like supplier power, highlighting the central role of liability composition in financial analysis and shareholder value determination.\",\"docName\":\"530_ent Analysis of Leverage and How It \",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:18:45.186\",\"fileName\":\"530_ent Analysis of Leverage and How It .pdf\",\"fileType\":\"pdf\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116821400489984\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Finance\",\"Data Analysis\",\"Research Paper\",\"Finance\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"19291f2d172a3fe88713e197cec0e9c0\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\530_ent Analysis of Leverage and How It .pdf\",\"priority\":\"20\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"da4d551e-a41f-48c5-8320-32efc0b3b2fb\",\"tokenNum\":\"6371\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:18:50.477\",\"description\":\"The document analyzes the prospects of the Chinese economy after the 2008 financial crisis, focusing on the rural consumption market. With transnational companies increasingly interested in China, the once saturated urban markets have shifted attention to rural areas. Following the crisis, the Chinese government implemented policies, such as providing rural families with subsidized home appliances, to stimulate rural consumption. Historically, China's growth relied heavily on investment and exports, while domestic consumption remained weak. Overreliance on investment has led to environmental issues, making increased consumption, especially in rural areas, crucial for sustainable growth. Research indicates that a 1% rise in consumption leads to a greater than 0.8% increase in GDP, highlighting its significance over investment-led growth. Rural areas, encompassing over 70% of China's population (700 million people), present vast untapped market potential. However, challenges persist: low income, lack of social security, price sensitivity, and limited demand for high-end goods dampen rural consumption. Policies like subsidized appliances provide short-term boosts but are insufficient for long-term growth. Sustainable development of the rural market requires raising rural incomes and improving social welfare systems, such as pensions, to encourage spending confidence. Despite current obstacles, the rural market offers significant opportunities for future economic expansion.\",\"docName\":\"568_cial crisis from the perspective of \",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:18:58.047\",\"fileName\":\"568_cial crisis from the perspective of .pdf\",\"fileType\":\"pdf\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116903361384448\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Finance\",\"Data Analysis\",\"Policy\",\"Finance\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"740a5bb31e0fc62e30d045e8dab8bdfa\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\568_cial crisis from the perspective of .pdf\",\"priority\":\"22\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"d5ff5da8-30a7-4c0c-b1bb-2cf50e68044b\",\"tokenNum\":\"805\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:18:57.161\",\"description\":\"This study examines the significance and construction of corporate culture in Chinese enterprises, highlighting its growing role in organizational development and competitiveness. Corporate culture is defined as a set of values, beliefs, attitudes, and behaviors that shape how a company operates and influences employee motivation, engagement, and productivity. Key challenges in building corporate culture include lack of distinctiveness, formalism, and misalignment with business systems. Effective corporate culture construction requires strong leadership, a people-oriented approach, adaptation to stages of enterprise growth, and integration with local and industry-specific characteristics. The process involves employee incentives, performance appraisal systems, fostering creativity, and aligning culture with societal values. Case studies of Chinese companies like Lenovo and Haier demonstrate successful models that blend international management practices with traditional Chinese values, emphasizing competition, cooperation, and continuous cultural development. The study concludes that corporate culture is vital for sustainable success and core competitiveness. It advocates for continuous consolidation and integration of diverse cultural elements. References underline the theoretical foundation and practical examples discussed in the paper.\",\"docName\":\"578_Construction  of  Corporate  Culture\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:19:09.511\",\"fileName\":\"578_Construction  of  Corporate  Culture.pdf\",\"fileType\":\"pdf\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116931396112384\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Research Paper\",\"Human Resources\",\"Case Study\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"0eda4a8df355c4ce0dfd1e45bf99f0a4\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\578_Construction  of  Corporate  Culture.pdf\",\"priority\":\"23\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"52d9dfee-2440-47ad-8741-5dff827967bc\",\"tokenNum\":\"4765\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:19:06.643\",\"description\":\"This Technical Compliance Statement and Safety Test Report certifies that the switching power supply product HF150W-SMF-X (with multiple model variations) from Hengfu Corporation has been tested according to the EN60950-1:2006 and its subsequent amendments. Testing was conducted by Audix Technology (Shanghai) Co., Ltd., TAF Accredited (No. 3238), under Safety Test Report No. ACI-L18004. The product complies with the safety requirements of the LVD directives 2014/35/EU based on a single sample evaluation. The report is signed by Deputy Manager Gilbert Wu and dated March 13, 2018. However, the certification does not guarantee the entire production line's compliance and prohibits use of the test lab logo. The report provides verification of technical safety compliance but is limited to the tested sample.\",\"docName\":\"584_pliance Statement Safety Test Report\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:19:11.637\",\"fileName\":\"584_pliance Statement Safety Test Report.pdf\",\"fileType\":\"pdf\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116971166502912\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Technology\",\"Report\",\"Compliance\",\"Technology\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"a572a03016e3f3d8ebe7ab35c8e43818\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\584_pliance Statement Safety Test Report.pdf\",\"priority\":\"24\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"c0764548-8f2d-4765-bcb9-5491413a31fa\",\"tokenNum\":\"294\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:19:10.398\",\"description\":\"This document compares basic education systems in the United States and China, analyzing reforms, structures, teaching methods, and outcomes. Both nations see education as pivotal for national development, but differ fundamentally in philosophy and practice. China's system is exam-oriented, stressing knowledge accumulation, discipline, and rote learning—producing diligent students with strong academic foundations but limited creativity and innovation. US education emphasizes student-centered learning, creativity, multicultural integration, flexible school management, and practical application of knowledge. US schools foster independence, provide humanistic environments, and offer diversified curricula and assessment methods. Teachers in the US require specialized certification and have autonomy in course design. Family involvement and lifelong reading are stressed in both systems, but the US places greater emphasis on individual development and equal educational access. China's recent reforms aim to reduce academic burdens, promote creativity, and internationalize education, while the US seeks to strengthen foundational skills. The document notes key differences: exam pressure and parental expectations are higher in China; US students enjoy freer environments and broader options, especially in secondary courses. Each system has strengths and shortcomings, with China's solid academic base contrasted against US innovation. For future improvement, both nations are encouraged to retain strengths while addressing weaknesses, aiming for balanced, quality mass education accessible to all.\",\"docName\":\"593_cation in theUnited Stated and China\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:19:27.817\",\"fileName\":\"593_cation in theUnited Stated and China.pdf\",\"fileType\":\"pdf\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996116986916114432\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Informational\",\"Research Paper\",\"Education\",\"Informational\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"b4e6a47f32104d1045ac773831bc0b38\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\593_cation in theUnited Stated and China.pdf\",\"priority\":\"25\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"8cd91c69-3361-4760-a450-b9bb33e448f6\",\"tokenNum\":\"10452\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:19:26.023\",\"description\":\"The document introduces Amy Tan, an American author known for her exploration of mother-daughter relationships and the Chinese-American experience. Tan, as a second-generation Chinese-American, brings a deep cultural perspective to her writing, with notable works including The Kitchen God’s Wife and Saving Fish from Drowning. Her most prominent novel, The Joy Luck Club, consists of sixteen interconnected stories detailing the lives of four Chinese immigrant mothers and their American-born daughters. The mothers, who escaped wartime China, form a club in America to maintain hope and connection. The narrative highlights generational and cultural conflicts: mothers retain traditional Chinese values while their daughters, raised in America, are highly Americanized and initially dismissive of their heritage. Examples, such as the strained relationship between Suyuan and her daughter Jingmei, illustrate the complex emotional conflicts exacerbated by language and cultural barriers. Despite years of disputes and misunderstandings, the daughters eventually gain insight into their mothers’ struggles and wisdom after facing their own challenges, leading to reconciliation and greater personal growth. The work underscores the difficulties and gradual resolution of mother-daughter and intercultural conflicts within immigrant families.\",\"docName\":\"A Brief Introduction of the Author\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:19:38.471\",\"fileName\":\"A Brief Introduction of the Author.docx\",\"fileType\":\"docx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996117052452114432\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Informational\",\"Case Study\",\"Informational\",\"Literature\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"4df0f9891d6457624b68a2944abedfbd\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\A Brief Introduction of the Author.docx\",\"priority\":\"26\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"648678c6-dd9a-4953-950f-30fd2b2bc835\",\"tokenNum\":\"595\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:19:37.433\",\"description\":\"This work provides an analytical comparison between ancient Greek and biblical perspectives on nature and history, examining how each tradition conceptualizes these themes. The study explores the critical role of historicity in the foundation and mission of the Church, and the theological implications of eschatology on its operation. Utilizing a critical, interpretive review of Greek and foreign literature, the treatise emphasizes the position of man as the central focus in theological inquiry. It discusses the detachment of humanity from transcendental purpose, resulting in spiritual and ontological decline. Christianity, however, offers an alternative view, enabling individuals to reassess their existence and identity within society. The treatise ultimately aims to present and advocate the essential message of theology: a revision of human existence wherein, from an eschatological standpoint, man is seen as eternal and capable of reestablishing a meaningful relationship with God by realizing his personal potential.\",\"docName\":\"A Comparison of the Natural and Historical Distinction Between Ancient Greece and the Bible.doc\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:19:48.664\",\"fileName\":\"A Comparison of the Natural and Historical Distinction Between Ancient Greece and the Bible.doc.docx\",\"fileType\":\"docx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996117100309123072\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"History\",\"Research Paper\",\"History\",\"Reference\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"f6b20e5386a4e4f9053ddaee3b0534f6\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\A Comparison of the Natural and Historical Distinction Between Ancient Greece and the Bible.doc.docx\",\"priority\":\"27\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"e74d920d-6f24-4021-a4b6-e7cc48250156\",\"tokenNum\":\"426\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:19:47.637\",\"description\":\"This BBC Learning English Weekender episode, hosted by Yvonne Archer, discusses the introduction of 'core British values' lessons in secondary schools in England, proposed as a government response to the London bombings. The initiative aims to foster a more united and cohesive society by encouraging respect, mutual understanding, and social harmony. Bill Rammell, Higher Education Minister, highlights fairness, democracy, and civic responsibility as essential British values, considering them intrinsic to the nation’s development. The program also explores perspectives from recent immigrants to England. Sun Chen from China emphasizes respect for history and heritage, citing well-maintained historical sites. Dima from Ukraine identifies devotion to democracy, freedom of speech, and a sense of duty to society (civic responsibility) as key values to be taught. Helen, also from China, considers respect for others, cultural understanding, and politeness as central to British society. The episode concludes by noting the variety of expressions and ideas associated with core British values, underscoring respect, politeness, and social responsibility as foundational principles for peaceful cohabitation and community integration.\",\"docName\":\"BBC-core-British-value\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:20:00.706\",\"fileName\":\"BBC-core-British-value.docx\",\"fileType\":\"docx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996117143107801088\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Informational\",\"Policy\",\"Education\",\"Informational\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"35c1c2e8ab39e371e0989687e6129686\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\BBC-core-British-value.docx\",\"priority\":\"28\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"68d42f4e-8799-4318-85b8-2cd4aa2ba359\",\"tokenNum\":\"1053\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:19:57.713\",\"description\":\"This document is a personal profile for Viola, detailing her educational and professional background, qualifications, and personal assessment. Viola will complete her diploma in Logistics Management in July 2012, with coursework in purchase and warehouse management, international trade, and related logistics operations. She has received significant achievements, including being named an excellent student and winning first prize in a logistics simulation competition in 2011. Viola is proficient in both English and Chinese, especially in business communication, and holds relevant certifications such as CET-4 (English) and CCT-1/National Computer Test Band 2 (computing). She is knowledgeable about logistics regulations and procedures and has strong office software skills. Her personal evaluation highlights communication skills, attention to detail, reliability, time management, and teamwork. Viola notes her commitment to learning, having focused primarily on her studies over the past two years, passing key tests, and gaining foundational knowledge in sports training. She expresses her readiness to apply her knowledge practically and requests an opportunity to demonstrate her abilities.\",\"docName\":\"Concise in English.2.doc\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:20:09.166\",\"fileName\":\"Concise in English.2.doc.docx\",\"fileType\":\"docx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996117185369608192\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Human Resources\",\"Education\",\"Resume\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"20bb0fbd9cd4c0a205e310d27b59dcec\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\Concise in English.2.doc.docx\",\"priority\":\"29\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"56a6a154-5bf5-4069-8fb4-492384d856f5\",\"tokenNum\":\"313\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:20:56.318\",\"description\":\"This paper analyzes U.S. innovation policy during two major crises—World War II and the COVID-19 pandemic. It surveys the U.S. government’s organization, funding, and management of crisis-driven research and development, focusing on the World War II Office of Scientific Research and Development (OSRD) and the COVID-19 response, including Operation Warp Speed (OWS) and BARDA. Key features of crisis innovation policy include prioritizing speed, top-down agenda-setting, concentrated funding to elite organizations, novel federal R&D contracts, patent policies balancing private incentives and public interest, and strong coordination between research, production, and end users. The WWII model achieved notable advances (e.g., radar, penicillin, atomic fission), shaped postwar science policy, and catalyzed geographic and sectoral innovation. The COVID-19 response, facing a much larger and more fragmented innovation system, emphasized rapid vaccine development with public-private partnerships and significant BARDA funding but had less centralized coordination for other public health innovations. The paper discusses four main policy tradeoffs: top-down vs. bottom-up priority setting, concentrated vs. distributed funding, tension between incentivizing innovation and broad diffusion via patents, and managing disruptions to the regular innovation system. It concludes that crisis innovation efforts can have long-term effects on innovation direction, R&D institutions, and technology policy, and that lessons from these experiences may inform responses to future crises requiring urgent, coordinated innovation.\",\"docName\":\"Deepin -NBER- Innovative policy in crises from World War II to COVID-19（英文）-2021\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:21:53.518\",\"fileName\":\"Deepin -NBER- Innovative policy in crises from World War II to COVID-19（英文）-2021.docx\",\"fileType\":\"docx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996117431176794112\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Data Analysis\",\"Policy\",\"Science\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"54c2c724ee6c67b2617ea8a7b4dce2cf\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\Deepin -NBER- Innovative policy in crises from World War II to COVID-19（英文）-2021.docx\",\"priority\":\"31\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"171f32aa-cff7-49fd-965d-5b7bcdc1e717\",\"tokenNum\":\"31371\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:21:49.692\",\"description\":\"This article presents the design and application of an intelligent brushless DC motor controller for electric bicycles, using the high-performance LPC2114 MCU as the core. The controller offers key functionalities including speed control, over-current and under-voltage protection, battery status indication, brake control with power cut-off, and soft start. The LPC2114’s features—16/32-bit ARM7TDMI-S CPU, integrated PWM, multiple A/D channels, and abundant I/O and interrupt resources—enable efficient acquisition and processing of motor position, speed, voltage, and current signals. The brushless DC motor structure, enhanced by Hall sensors, achieves high reliability, efficiency, and ease of maintenance, making it superior to traditional motors and ideal for electric bicycles. The controller's hardware integrates MOSFET drivers for phase switching and ensures fail-safe operation by locking the inverter bridge under fault conditions. The software employs modular and structured programming, with main and interrupt routines managing core functions. Key design challenges addressed include reliable rotor position sampling, smooth speed modulation using PWM, noise reduction during phase transitions, and locked-rotor protection. Experimental validation with a 48V/350W motor demonstrated excellent performance: stable speed regulation, minimal steady-state error (<2.0%), and fast response time (~4.5s). The proposed LPC2114-based controller reduces system complexity, cost, and PCB space, making it suitable for production electric bicycles and supporting the trend toward cleaner, more efficient urban transport.\",\"docName\":\"Design of Electric Bicycle Controller.doc\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:22:04.939\",\"fileName\":\"Design of Electric Bicycle Controller.doc.docx\",\"fileType\":\"docx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996117655043575808\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Technology\",\"Engineering\",\"Specifications\",\"Technology\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"d0587c36f914155ccf4660ab0caea406\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\Design of Electric Bicycle Controller.doc.docx\",\"priority\":\"32\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"4bb25993-82c1-4a3a-8487-2b2fe0d34cab\",\"tokenNum\":\"3207\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:22:03.600\",\"description\":\"This article introduces a hardware accelerator for Monte Carlo simulation sampling—the Electron Tunnelling Noise Programmable Random Variate Accelerator (PRVA). Deployed on a Digilent Arty-100T FPGA using the LiteX framework and a FemtoRV RISC-V soft processor, the PRVA leverages analog electron tunneling noise (via a reverse-biased Zener diode and XADC) to generate random samples from arbitrary univariate distributions, including mixtures of Gaussians. Compared to the GNU Scientific Library’s random number generators, the PRVA achieves average and median benchmark speedups of 8.70× and 8.69×, respectively, owing to benchmarks spending about 90% of execution time in sample generation. The output’s accuracy is quantified with Wasserstein distance ratios (mean 1.48×) relative to software methods. The PRVA can flexibly support various FPGA boards with XADC, offering high speed (492 Mb/s), low power consumption (1.983 W combined), and programmable distribution capabilities. Implementation details cover the analog circuit design and temperature dependence compensation. Benchmarking spans twelve C applications. The PRVA outperformed prior accelerators in speed and efficiency; its principal limitation is ADC sampling rate. Related research is discussed, comparing multiple random variate generation methods. The PRVA enables efficient, flexible Monte Carlo sampling, addressing the limitations of both conventional pseudorandom generators and traditional hardware under stagnating Moore’s law.\",\"docName\":\"Electron-Tunnelling-Noise Programmable Random\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:22:16.705\",\"fileName\":\"Electron-Tunnelling-Noise Programmable Random.pdf\",\"fileType\":\"pdf\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996117713377955840\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Data Analysis\",\"Research Paper\",\"Engineering\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"d2934284a7701af023a0b904d41322eb\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\Electron-Tunnelling-Noise Programmable Random.pdf\",\"priority\":\"33\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"0afdab15-6c3e-4b13-8e3d-a9cb35feebca\",\"tokenNum\":\"9161\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:22:14.985\",\"description\":\"This document is a comprehensive sample Request for Proposal (RFP) for selecting an Electronic Medical Record (EMR) system for a healthcare organization. It outlines the purpose, background, and goals of the EMR selection, including a list of service offerings such as primary care, emergency care, behavioral health, and more. The RFP specifies the scope—primarily focused on ambulatory EMR, practice management, and billing, with potential extensions to document imaging, data warehousing, and related technologies. Instructions are provided for proposal submission, including response structure, evaluation criteria, timetable, confidentiality terms, and communication protocols. Vendors are required to address detailed general, functional, operational, and technical requirements, primarily via an accompanying Excel workbook. They must provide comprehensive project cost breakdowns (hardware, software, integration, implementation, training, and recurring costs), staffing plans, company information, reference clients, and authorized signatures. The evaluation process features multiple stages, including initial proposal review, onsite demonstrations, and reference checks. Criteria for selection include system integration, track record, total cost of ownership, technical foundation, implementation plan, and future development. Strict guidelines are set for response format, requirement coverage, and handling exceptions. The document underscores the need for confidentiality and reserves the organization’s right to reject proposals or negotiate terms. Overall, it serves as a structured template to obtain thorough and comparable proposals from healthcare IT vendors for an EMR solution.\",\"docName\":\"Electronic Medical Record System Selection Proposal\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:22:28.105\",\"fileName\":\"Electronic Medical Record System Selection Proposal.pdf\",\"fileType\":\"pdf\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996117761130106880\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Technology\",\"Proposal\",\"Technology\",\"Healthcare\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"a40b7a75e8fa6a9f4784d266f11d9ad5\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\Electronic Medical Record System Selection Proposal.pdf\",\"priority\":\"34\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"93597f59-a417-421a-bbde-c196045240fd\",\"tokenNum\":\"5494\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:22:26.752\",\"description\":\"The document outlines the education and professional experiences of an individual seeking a sales and marketing position. Currently, the candidate is an intern at China Galaxy Securities’ Investment Banking Department in Beijing, where they assist in market analysis for major projects such as the Bank of China’s IPO and perform research on the domestic bond market, including translating proposals for the Asian Development Bank. Prior experience includes working as an operation assistant with CCTV-4’s Happy China Program, where they selected foreign talent and gained significant interpersonal skills, as well as teaching spoken English at New Thinking Spoken English Training Center, where they developed innovative teaching methods and received an award for excellence. The candidate is pursuing a Bachelor of Science in Finance at Beijing Language and Culture University, maintaining a 4.0 GPA and expected to graduate in July 2011. They have held leadership roles, such as President of the Student Council in high school, and have received multiple scholarships and honors for academic and extracurricular achievements. Their language skills include passing national English proficiency tests at high levels and earning the Financial English Certificate Test Level A, with advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office tools. Personal interests include psychology, pedagogics, music, dance, and literature.\",\"docName\":\"English resume.2.doc\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:23:50.480\",\"fileName\":\"English resume.2.doc.docx\",\"fileType\":\"docx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996117810484482048\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Education\",\"Resume\",\"Marketing\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"cb6d6f22faef1d901418864a2203a7d2\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\English resume.2.doc.docx\",\"priority\":\"35\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"819aed79-290b-4c1b-a167-bdcd470f3675\",\"tokenNum\":\"540\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:22:43.977\",\"description\":\"This paper analyzes efficient risk-sharing arrangements in economies where coalitions of agents may form and deviate, focusing on the implications of 'social capital'—the ability to coordinate beliefs about future cooperation—on the sustainability of self-enforcing insurance institutions. The authors show that higher social capital improves the formation of Pareto-improving risk-sharing coalitions but simultaneously tightens incentive constraints, as not just the initial coalition but also potential deviating coalitions can more easily coordinate and enforce social norms. The model employs a cooperative game-theoretic approach and an equilibrium notion where allocations are robust to coalitional deviations, with the value of the outside option (what defectors can guarantee themselves) endogenously determined. Key theoretical findings include: (1) For low to moderate social capital, coalition formation increases welfare and provides partial or full insurance; as social capital rises, incentive constraints bind, and equilibrium allocations become less generous; (2) For very high social capital, full insurance is impossible—equilibrium requires 'utility burning' (inefficiency or waste) to deter defection, yielding diminished gains from risk sharing; (3) The effect of social capital is non-monotonic: higher trust can paradoxically lower achievable insurance due to the threat of organized defection. The study provides both analytic and numerical characterizations of equilibrium allocations, comparative statics, and relates findings to literature on limited enforcement, coalition-proof equilibria, and social capital. The results highlight the complex interplay between belief coordination, risk sharing, and institutional design.\",\"docName\":\"NBER National Bureau of Economic Research64页_649kb\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:24:00.266\",\"fileName\":\"NBER National Bureau of Economic Research64页_649kb.docx\",\"fileType\":\"docx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996117882731368448\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Finance\",\"Data Analysis\",\"Research Paper\",\"Finance\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"570a1ae43c49f779bfbb01c6e8c365ac\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\NBER National Bureau of Economic Research64页_649kb.docx\",\"priority\":\"37\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"a3f6519c-9c24-4952-b62a-b8b6181d93e2\",\"tokenNum\":\"27093\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:23:55.798\",\"description\":\"This paper examines the use of ChatGPT, a large language model, to extract managerial expectations of corporate policies—particularly investment plans—from the textual content of nearly 75,000 US public company earnings call transcripts (2006–2020). The authors develop a 'ChatGPT Investment Score' by prompting the model to classify anticipated changes in capital expenditure, then validate it against Duke CFO Survey responses and show strong correlation. The score predicts future physical, intangible, and R&D investments up to nine quarters ahead, offering incremental information beyond established financial metrics like Tobin’s q. The score also negatively forecasts firms’ future abnormal stock returns, consistent with investment-based asset pricing theory, suggesting that standard market prices do not fully incorporate managers’ disclosed expectations—even when publicly available. Predictive power is greatest for smaller firms, those in early product lifecycle stages, and those in competitive industries. Additional corporate policies (dividends, employment) are similarly extracted and validated. Robustness checks, out-of-sample tests, and masking experiments confirm the findings. ChatGPT outperforms traditional models (e.g., RoBERTa) in extracting nuanced managerial expectations. The study demonstrates that AI can efficiently produce interpretable and predictive measures of corporate outlook, complementing or enhancing traditional executive surveys and informing investors and policymakers. This creates new opportunities for large-scale, real-time financial analysis and decision support using AI-driven text analysis.\",\"docName\":\"NBER-ChatGPT and Company Policy - UK-68页_706kb\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:25:06.361\",\"fileName\":\"NBER-ChatGPT and Company Policy - UK-68页_706kb.docx\",\"fileType\":\"docx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996118183970476032\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Finance\",\"Data Analysis\",\"Technology\",\"Finance\",\"Technology\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"612ccf1a4320981c7f85609b3c6f143d\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\NBER-ChatGPT and Company Policy - UK-68页_706kb.docx\",\"priority\":\"38\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"1e12463c-32fa-4fb1-9011-e75a8afc9685\",\"tokenNum\":\"35897\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:25:03.937\",\"description\":\"This document presents a multilevel modelling approach for monitoring and simulating train-passing events on the IB5 Staffordshire rail bridge using streaming telemetry data. The study leverages a comprehensive sensing system—including fibre Bragg gratings and accelerometers—to collect high-frequency strain data during each train crossing. The work proposes a hierarchical (multilevel) Gaussian process model, with a low-rank approximation, designed to capture the characteristic and event-specific strain responses for different commuter train types (350 and 22x) identified via a decision tree using BWIM (Bridge Weigh In Motion) data features (axle number, weight, spacing). The model encodes domain knowledge via boundary condition constraints and employs Bayesian inference techniques for uncertainty quantification. Key innovations include modeling repeated, highly comparable train events as longitudinal data, implementing a basis function approximation for scalable Gaussian process inference, and constructing interpretable correlation structures for outlier and novelty detection. The model demonstrates effectiveness in distinguishing train types, identifying anomalous events, and is proposed as a foundation for digital twin simulations to study previously unobserved scenarios (e.g., different train types or payloads). Future work aims to develop richer mean functions and basis representations for further insight and simulation capability. The research contributes to the practical deployment of digital twins for structural health monitoring in critical transport infrastructure.\",\"docName\":\"Towards Multilevel Modelling of Train\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:25:16.580\",\"fileName\":\"Towards Multilevel Modelling of Train.pdf\",\"fileType\":\"pdf\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996118469766156288\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Data Analysis\",\"Research Paper\",\"Engineering\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"c649df3ebb2a1957c7c8e01350076afc\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\Towards Multilevel Modelling of Train.pdf\",\"priority\":\"39\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"f3caf18b-5315-4af1-b4e3-621ce4b64df4\",\"tokenNum\":\"5965\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:25:15.500\",\"description\":\"The Jingxi Ancient Road, located west of Beijing, offers travelers a historical and scenic hiking experience, tracing ancient merchant routes through mountainous landscapes. This detailed travelogue describes a one-day trek along the Wangping Ancient Road, starting from Beijing's Pingguoyuan Subway Station, transferring via bus 929 to Shiguyan Village. The 12-kilometer hike traverses well-preserved stone paths marked by horse hoof prints and passes through historic villages such as Daoxu and Magezhuang, notable sites including Ma Zhiyuan’s residence and Sanyi Temple, and ascends Niujiaoling Pass, known for stunning mountain views and Buddhist cliff carvings. The journey ends at Longjiazhuang Village, with easy bus connections back to the city. Other recommended routes in the Jingxi network include the Yuhe Ancient Road (15 km, ending at Tanzhe Temple), the Lutan Ancient Road (8 km loop near Jietai Temple), and hikes around Cuandixia Village. Hikes typically range from 3 to 7 hours, with low to moderate difficulty, suitable for most fitness levels. Practical tips include wearing comfortable shoes, bringing water and snacks, dressing in layers, carrying maps or GPS, and choosing the season for ideal scenery. The trek offers a blend of history, culture, and nature, making it a unique excursion from Beijing. Sources referenced include travelchinaguide.com, easytourchina.com, chinacultureplus.com, and beijing.gov.cn.\",\"docName\":\"[Dan's Travel Journal] A Journey Back in Time on the Jingxi Ancient Road 1\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:25:23.245\",\"fileName\":\"[Dan's Travel Journal] A Journey Back in Time on the Jingxi Ancient Road 1.pdf\",\"fileType\":\"pdf\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996118518264893440\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Informational\",\"History\",\"Informational\",\"History\",\"Travel Guide\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-11-19T18:32:32\",\"md5\":\"7067b745bcb6daa140de479be58ba40f\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\[Dan's Travel Journal] A Journey Back in Time on the Jingxi Ancient Road 1.pdf\",\"priority\":\"40\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"f0e678a3-e378-497f-a14b-ddba06bf6f44\",\"tokenNum\":\"1307\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:25:22.398\",\"description\":\"The 2022 Directors’ Liability Survey Report by WTW and Clyde & Co offers a comprehensive global view of Directors and Officers (D&O) risk perceptions, compiling insights from respondents in over 40 countries. The top risks identified for directors globally are cyber attacks, data loss, cyber extortion, regulatory threats (including fines and penalties), and health and safety/environmental prosecutions, though regional differences exist in priority and severity. Climate change, while not in the universal top five, is a significant and rising concern, especially within finance, insurance, and energy sectors. The surge in cyber extortion and ransomware drove capacity and premium challenges in the insurance market; ransomware attacks have increased 200% since 2019. Regional analysis highlights differing emphases, such as economic climate risks in Latin America, regulatory activism in Asia, and class actions in Australasia. The use of alternative risk transfer mechanisms, like captives or personal guarantees, is growing but remains limited in adoption. Trends in class actions show a decline in the US but an uptick in SPAC- and ESG-related filings worldwide, with regulatory scrutiny and whistleblowing also increasing, especially in North America. The impact of COVID-19 persists, influencing risks such as employment litigation and operational resilience. The report identifies a continual escalation in regulatory demands and enforcement activity, highlighting the necessity for robust risk management and disclosure practices for directors and officers globally.\",\"docName\":\"《2022年董事责任险调查报告》（英文）-58页_3mb\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:25:45.755\",\"fileName\":\"《2022年董事责任险调查报告》（英文）-58页_3mb.pptx\",\"fileType\":\"pptx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996118547197202432\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Finance\",\"Legal\",\"Compliance\",\"Finance\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"319c21ed95e145375e2ca22e7dc6400f\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\《2022年董事责任险调查报告》（英文）-58页_3mb.pptx\",\"priority\":\"41\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"1a3475e9-ca7f-42df-ad93-f1ce1cd27250\",\"tokenNum\":\"28754\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:25:43.684\",\"description\":\"The Accenture Technology Vision 2022 report, titled 'Meet Me in the Metaverse,' explores how emerging digital technologies are redefining business and society. The centerpiece is the 'Metaverse Continuum'—an evolving spectrum of digitally enhanced realities transforming the ways businesses operate, serve customers, and structure work. The report identifies four key trends: 1) WebMe—reimagining the internet through immersive metaverse and Web3 solutions, driving greater personalization, interoperability, and a need for new digital strategies for enterprises; 2) Programmable World—embedding advanced technologies like IoT, digital twins, and AR/VR into physical environments to unlock unprecedented automation, customization, and new business models; 3) The Unreal—addressing the blending of authentic and synthetic content due to advances in AI, with a focus on driving trust and authenticity amidst deepfakes and bias; and 4) Computing the Impossible—leveraging next-generation computing (quantum, HPC, bio-inspired) to solve previously intractable problems, enabling disruptive innovation across industries. The report emphasizes the urgency for leaders to act—developing new strategies, talent pipelines, technical infrastructure, and partnerships to remain future-ready. It outlines both significant opportunities and risks around interoperability, data privacy, cyber-security, policy, and ethical considerations. Drawing on global surveys and expert analysis, Accenture argues that proactive engagement with these trends will determine which enterprises shape tomorrow’s digital world.\",\"docName\":\"《技术展望2022》英文版_97页_6mb\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:26:17.870\",\"fileName\":\"《技术展望2022》英文版_97页_6mb.pptx\",\"fileType\":\"pptx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996118636477157376\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Research Paper\",\"Technology\",\"Report\",\"Technology\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"9fbefd1c71099a86dab1fd35ae4ae8de\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\《技术展望2022》英文版_97页_6mb.pptx\",\"priority\":\"42\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"483eb96f-c24b-467c-8be3-8980bbd89dbc\",\"tokenNum\":\"45343\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:26:13.766\",\"description\":\"This document summarizes a Gartner webinar focused on their 5-Phase Approach for Enterprise Architecture (EA) Leaders to master AI implementation. The approach aims to ensure AI initiatives align with targeted business outcomes through structured, outcome-driven planning. The five phases are: (1) Align AI initiatives with business capability-based outcomes; (2) Assess maturity of information architecture to support necessary data aggregation; (3) Use design thinking to select AI models appropriate for specific initiatives; (4) Collaborate with analytics and engineering teams to establish robust training, testing, and deployment practices; and (5) Define triggers and controls for monitoring model drift and ongoing business value. The framework stresses the importance of data usability, incremental capability mapping, and emphasizes AI TRiSM—a system for managing trust, risk, and security throughout the AI lifecycle. Performance, operational, and compliance metrics are highlighted to ensure continued business value and mitigate negative outcomes, such as model failure or value drift. The webinar also references practical examples and conference details for further professional development. Legal, compliance, and participation guidelines are noted, with reminders that Gartner’s material is proprietary and distribution is restricted.\",\"docName\":\"【会议演讲PPT】Gartner++企业架构领导者掌握+AI+的5+阶段方法-英-49页_2mb\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:26:20.819\",\"fileName\":\"【会议演讲PPT】Gartner++企业架构领导者掌握+AI+的5+阶段方法-英-49页_2mb.pptx\",\"fileType\":\"pptx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996118762650210304\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Technology\",\"Specifications\",\"Technology\",\"Training\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"cb87b59180c99d65e608076102b3352c\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\【会议演讲PPT】Gartner++企业架构领导者掌握+AI+的5+阶段方法-英-49页_2mb.pptx\",\"priority\":\"43\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"8d0f7117-1a75-470f-9f91-4ffec4bd231c\",\"tokenNum\":\"3126\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:26:19.784\",\"description\":\"This Gartner webinar highlights the growing impact and business value of AI services, especially generative AI (GenAI), across various industries. Key findings include significant operational improvements such as TCS saving $2.1 million, Hexaware saving 50,000+ hours, HCL achieving 2.7x throughput, and Salesforce increasing live chat by 450%. GenAI’s share of AI services revenue is projected to reach 42% by 2027 ($443bn total), with vertical/domain-specific models expected to exceed half of enterprise usage. Top GenAI use cases are content creation, customer experience enhancement, knowledge management, and industry-specific solutions in healthcare, manufacturing, retail, financial services, communications, and energy. The Gartner AI TRiSM framework addresses AI risks in areas such as explainability, model monitoring, security, and privacy. Providers are tackling challenges of data-readiness and skill gaps, investing in custom models, new tech architectures, and responsible AI practices. Major recommendations include building AI centers of excellence, prioritizing high-ROI use cases like summarization and knowledge management, and co-creating industry-tailored solutions. Upcoming research focuses on GenAI’s emerging use cases, business value patterns, challenges, and forecasts for AI services. The webinar also promotes Gartner’s Tech Growth & Innovation Conference and emphasizes strategies for leveraging AI to drive sustainable business growth, improve product experiences, and optimize processes.\",\"docName\":\"【会议演讲PPT】Gartner+通过+AI+服务和解决方案实现业务价值-英-42页_1mb\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:26:26.965\",\"fileName\":\"【会议演讲PPT】Gartner+通过+AI+服务和解决方案实现业务价值-英-42页_1mb.pptx\",\"fileType\":\"pptx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996118787891531776\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Research Paper\",\"Technology\",\"Technology\",\"Industry/Domain Solutions\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"70c9a3954942e5a520bfca3e0558fa79\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\【会议演讲PPT】Gartner+通过+AI+服务和解决方案实现业务价值-英-42页_1mb.pptx\",\"priority\":\"44\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"762c3e82-df4e-4d99-931b-b785857f1799\",\"tokenNum\":\"4147\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:26:26.171\",\"description\":\"Yunnan paiyao, a Chinese herbal mixture developed in the early 1900s in Yunnan province, gained international attention during the Vietnam War for its reputed ability to stop bleeding. Its key ingredient is Panax notoginseng (notoginseng), known for potent hemostatic properties, though formulas vary and may include myrrh, ox bile, Chinese yam, and other botanicals. The product often includes a distinct red 'hit pill' intended for severe wounds, believed to contain a concentrated dose of notoginseng. Scientific studies confirm that Yunnan paiyao and notoginseng can significantly reduce bleeding times, though the mechanisms remain poorly understood. Additional pharmacological actions include estrogen-like activity and fibrinogen reduction. Veterinary use is reported, mainly to limit bleeding in surgeries and in cancer treatments, but clinical evidence is limited. Risks include contraindication in pregnancy (oral use), potential bone marrow toxicity at high doses, and serious concerns over contamination (heavy metals, pesticides, adulterants) due to lack of manufacturing standards. Pesticide residues, especially organochlorines like DDT, have been detected, leading to occasional import restrictions. Overall, Yunnan paiyao demonstrates promising hemostatic benefits but is hampered by lack of comprehensive scientific validation, unclear mechanisms, inconsistent quality, and safety concerns.\",\"docName\":\"对云南白药的英文综述\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:26:33.732\",\"fileName\":\"对云南白药的英文综述.pdf\",\"fileType\":\"pdf\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996118814680551424\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Compliance\",\"Science\",\"Healthcare\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"7169cddcdfd21396967aae7a2ea74c6a\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\对云南白药的英文综述.pdf\",\"priority\":\"45\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"9c9f466d-9a69-4c75-b436-dcec730ded85\",\"tokenNum\":\"2600\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:26:33.081\",\"description\":\"This report analyzes the post-pandemic outlook for European industries, highlighting the need for reinvention to secure global competitiveness. European companies excel in sustainability but lag behind U.S. and Asian peers in digital acceleration, particularly in Technology and Software sectors. Key drivers for future success include business resilience, regionalization, industry convergence, digital transformation, and sustainability—the 'twin transformation.' Strategic recommendations center on three critical actions: 1) building cross-industry ecosystems to foster innovation, 2) accelerating combined digital and sustainable investments, and 3) aggressively reskilling the workforce to address skills gaps and support employment growth. Survey results from 700 C-suite executives in 13 countries point to high confidence in recovery, yet emphasize urgent action is needed, especially with investment in AI, 5G, and hybrid cloud technologies. European industries hold strong leadership in Automotive, Consumer Goods, and Life Sciences, but must boost R&D and start-up investment to keep pace in high-growth areas like Smart Manufacturing, Digital Health, and Smart Mobility. Policy recommendations urge the EU and member states to facilitate regulation, incentivize R&D, strengthen education and training, and promote collaborative public-private partnerships and industry ecosystems. The report forecasts the twin transformation could create up to 5 million net jobs by 2030. Dialogue and coordination at the European level are seen as key to supporting industrial reinvention, accelerating digital and sustainability transitions, and building next-generation workforce capabilities.\",\"docName\":\"深度-埃森哲-报告：重塑行业以提升未来竞争力（英文）-2021.6-59页_14mb\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:26:46.062\",\"fileName\":\"深度-埃森哲-报告：重塑行业以提升未来竞争力（英文）-2021.6-59页_14mb.pptx\",\"fileType\":\"pptx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996118843663192064\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Technology\",\"Policy\",\"Technology\",\"Industry\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"7cf15ce0b669b7e388307ff5b91d00d8\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\深度-埃森哲-报告：重塑行业以提升未来竞争力（英文）-2021.6-59页_14mb.pptx\",\"priority\":\"46\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"ccc06a24-7c52-47e7-9568-345356639ba0\",\"tokenNum\":\"15063\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:26:44.554\",\"description\":\"This document contains two sample English resumes for international students seeking administrative roles. Ben Parker’s resume highlights his experience as a Front Office Coordinator at SN Group Association (2007-present) and prior role as a Receptionist at Right Choice Tech Co. (2005-2007). His responsibilities include managing front desk operations, handling appointments, client communication, and document processing. Ben’s key skills feature strong management, organizational and communication abilities, proficiency in MS Office applications, multitasking, and dictation at 76 wpm. His educational background is a high school graduation from Maryland College, Hamilton, Ohio, with references provided. The second resume is for Mathew Hederson, who seeks a Word Processor position. He has worked at Hugen Grant University (2007-present) and served as Assistant Word Processor at Oasis College (2005-2007). Mathew’s tasks involve data entry, word processing, organizing and manipulating data, equipment management, and scheduling, with skills in keyboarding (40 wpm), data evaluation, PC applications, and bilingual proficiency in Latin. He holds a high school diploma from Greenland College, Georgia, and provides a reference. Both resumes focus on administrative skills, proficiency with office technology, and prior experience.\",\"docName\":\"留学生英文简历模板\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:26:51.881\",\"fileName\":\"留学生英文简历模板.pdf\",\"fileType\":\"pdf\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996118891784441856\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Text Document\",\"Human Resources\",\"Reference\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"e0d000785e00fd816bdafd0c9ca13540\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\留学生英文简历模板.pdf\",\"priority\":\"47\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"cadb14d8-9b8e-4c0f-b47e-f064658063ce\",\"tokenNum\":\"855\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:26:50.915\",\"description\":\"China has reported 264,302 HIV/AIDS cases, with health authorities estimating about 700,000 infected individuals nationwide—440,000 of whom may be unaware of their status. At the American Public Health Association conference in San Francisco, Terry Tian, M.P.H., presented a collaborative project exploring community-based organizations' capacity to support community health research. The project involved CIRA, the Community Alliance for Research and Engagement, The Institute for Community Research, and partnered health centers in Connecticut, aiming to assess organizational research activities and requirements via a newly developed survey. The Pilot Projects in HIV/AIDS Prevention Research program facilitates rapid response to developments in HIV/AIDS research and provides preliminary results for grant applications. HIV/AIDS is primarily transmitted through sexual contact, blood (including unsterilized needles and medical instruments), and mother-to-child routes (placenta, delivery, breastfeeding). CIRA will participate in the XIX International AIDS Conference in Washington, D.C., with sessions on topics such as HIV in correctional settings. World AIDS Day is observed globally on February 1, with volunteers and public figures actively contributing to awareness and support, including caring for HIV/AIDS patients and orphans. The global community continues to strive toward eradicating AIDS.\",\"docName\":\"艾滋病英文ppt\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:26:59.510\",\"fileName\":\"艾滋病英文ppt.pptx\",\"fileType\":\"pptx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996118918464409600\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Research Paper\",\"Healthcare\",\"Conference\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"2c0c0fa2653e26f1e2fbd433927d832c\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\艾滋病英文ppt.pptx\",\"priority\":\"48\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"34ff3871-6bb8-4383-9381-0c2ca800a0b8\",\"tokenNum\":\"717\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:26:57.773\",\"description\":\"The document presents Alibaba Group's financial and operational results for the March quarter and fiscal year 2020. In fiscal 2020, Alibaba achieved over US$1 trillion GMV, with annual revenue rising 35% YoY to RMB509.7 billion (US$72.0 billion) and core commerce revenue up 35%. Adjusted EBITA rose 28% YoY to RMB137.1 billion, while cloud computing revenue surged 62% YoY to RMB40.0 billion, though it posted an EBITA loss. The COVID-19 pandemic impacted segments differently: retail GMV and Tmall online physical goods grew, while local services like Ele.me suffered but rebounded as lockdowns eased. Accelerated digital transformation was noted, including increased adoption of cloud, DingTalk (with 155 million daily users in March), and grocery delivery. Alibaba undertook substantial social responsibility actions, donating over 200 million PPE units globally and supporting medical and employment initiatives. Free cash flow for FY2020 grew 25% to RMB130.9 billion (US$18.5 billion), though the March 2020 quarter saw an outflow due to AliExpress payment restructuring. Net income dropped 88% YoY for the March quarter, mainly from investment losses, but non-GAAP net income rose 12%. Alibaba consolidated a 33% equity stake in Ant Financial, increasing its share of profits. The company reports continued strong profitability, cash generation, and growth in digital services, despite pandemic-related operational challenges and volatility in investment valuations.\",\"docName\":\"阿里巴巴-2020年第一季度及全年阿里集团财报PPT（英文）-2020.5-25页_1mb\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:27:06.860\",\"fileName\":\"阿里巴巴-2020年第一季度及全年阿里集团财报PPT（英文）-2020.5-25页_1mb.pptx\",\"fileType\":\"pptx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996118947228946432\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Finance\",\"Compliance\",\"Reporting\",\"Finance\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"352b625c5c1de2ea91051ed0f400e948\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\阿里巴巴-2020年第一季度及全年阿里集团财报PPT（英文）-2020.5-25页_1mb.pptx\",\"priority\":\"49\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"e82fcfb0-2b52-49bd-bb26-671b33e659da\",\"tokenNum\":\"8837\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:27:05.809\",\"description\":\"The June Quarter 2019 results for Alibaba report robust financial performance, with total revenue reaching RMB114,924 million (US$16,741 million), representing a 42% year-over-year (YoY) increase. Core commerce contributed 87% of revenue and grew by 44% YoY, driven by strong China retail, Ele.me, and cloud computing segments. Cloud computing revenue surged 66% YoY, and digital media and entertainment rose 6% YoY. Annual active consumers hit 674 million, with 755 million mobile MAUs. Core commerce adjusted EBITA increased 25% YoY to RMB41,025 million (US$5,976 million), and marketplace-based core commerce adjusted EBITA rose 27% YoY to RMB46,800 million (US$6,817 million). While cloud computing, digital media, and innovation segments reported adjusted EBITA losses, strong core commerce profitability supports continued investment. Operating cash flow was RMB34,612 million (US$5,042 million), down 4% YoY, and free cash flow reached RMB26,361 million (US$3,840 million). Costs for sales & marketing, product development, and general & administrative expenses remained stable as a percentage of revenue. The report includes non-GAAP measures, reconciled with GAAP, with non-GAAP net income at RMB30,949 million (US$4,508 million). Segment reporting and risk factors are detailed, emphasizing strategic growth areas and possible uncertainties. Cash, cash equivalents, and short-term investments stood at RMB212,189 million (US$30,909 million).\",\"docName\":\"阿里巴巴-2020财年第一季度阿里巴巴财报PPT（英文）-2019.8.15-13页_2mb\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:27:13.192\",\"fileName\":\"阿里巴巴-2020财年第一季度阿里巴巴财报PPT（英文）-2019.8.15-13页_2mb.pptx\",\"fileType\":\"pptx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996118980934373376\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Finance\",\"Reporting\",\"Finance\",\"Spreadsheet\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"b32d2238e6e29da3762cc2c1881ed96c\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\阿里巴巴-2020财年第一季度阿里巴巴财报PPT（英文）-2019.8.15-13页_2mb.pptx\",\"priority\":\"50\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"f1245fd5-aea7-4556-b80a-d646e2dc1d30\",\"tokenNum\":\"3508\",\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"author\":\"\",\"createTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:27:12.369\",\"description\":\"This document is an English resume template for Zheng Yan, seeking a challenging software engineer position focused on software design and development. The candidate holds a Master of Engineering from Tsinghua University (1997-2000) and a Bachelor of Engineering from Beijing Institute of Technology (1993-1997), both in Automation. Core academic subjects include mathematics (e.g., probability, linear algebra) and electronics/computer-related courses (e.g., data structures, artificial intelligence). The candidate demonstrates proficiency in various programming languages and tools, including MS Frontpage, JavaBeans, HTML, CGI, JavaScript, Perl, C, C++, Pascal, PL/I, SQL, and more. English proficiency is evidenced by passing CET-6, TOEFL (623), and GRE (2213). Awards include the Guanghua First-class Scholarship, the Metal Machining Practice Award, and an Academic Progress Award. Additional qualifications reflect business knowledge in financial and healthcare domains, a strong interest in the internet, and sound common sense.\",\"docName\":\"陈述型英文简历模板\",\"editTime\":\"2025-12-03T15:27:18.702\",\"fileName\":\"陈述型英文简历模板.pdf\",\"fileType\":\"pdf\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\",\"id\":\"1996119008449007616\",\"isDeleted\":\"0\",\"isTmpFile\":\"false\",\"labelNameList\":[\"Technology\",\"Technology\",\"Education\",\"Resume\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-12-03T06:00:00\",\"md5\":\"c66190b8c3333003ae6e8b35033173b2\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\yangl\\\\Desktop\\\\ZBW\\\\Local-test\\\\Local-solution\\\\KBQA_Reg\\\\陈述型英文简历模板.pdf\",\"priority\":\"51\",\"score\":\"0.0\",\"source\":\"LOCAL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"syncId\":\"dd24db14-0c62-4fb8-8d22-5223f4190fe3\",\"tokenNum\":\"372\",\"uriPath\":\"\"}]"}}
